// Change: new rule
// Title: HackTool - Coercer Tools Execution - Linux
// Sigma ID: 4c3b2a1f-0e9d-8c7b-6a5f-4e3d2c1b0a9e
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: Swachchhanda Shrawan Poudel (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2026-04-21 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: credential-access, collection, T1187, T1557.001
// Description: Detects execution of DFSCoerce and Coercer, tools that abuse the MS-DFSNM and other RPC
//   interfaces to coerce Windows hosts into authenticating to an attacker-controlled machine via
//   NTLM. The captured authentication can be relayed (e.g. via ntlmrelayx) or cracked offline.
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://github.com/n00py/Outpacket#7-auth-coercion
//   - https://github.com/p0dalirius/Coercer
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/6b9ade7935a13d35a57e75ff2587fbedcc53ef56/rules/linux/process_creation/proc_creation_lnx_hktl_coerce_tools.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ((FolderPath contains "/dfscoerce" or FolderPath contains "/coercer" or FolderPath contains "/ShadowCoerce" or FolderPath contains "/CredCoerce") or (ProcessCommandLine contains "Coerce" and ProcessCommandLine contains "-u" and ProcessCommandLine contains "-p")) or ((FolderPath contains "/python" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName contains "python") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "dfscoerce" or ProcessCommandLine contains "Coercer" or ProcessCommandLine contains "ShadowCoerce" or ProcessCommandLine contains "CredCoerce"))
